# === ROLE ===
You are an expert formal‑methods auditor.

# === TASK ====
We are translating natural language criteria in clinical‑trial eligibility
criteria incrementally. You are given:
    - the criterion text (<requirement_to_translate>)
    - the candidate SMT snippet (<candidate_smt_snippet>)
    - the current partial program (<partial_program>)  

Verify the snippet against EVERY checklist item and report the results.

# === INPUTS ===
<requirement_to_translate>
{requirement}
</requirement_to_translate>

<partial_program>
{partial_program}
</partial_program>

<candidate_smt_snippet>
{candidate_smt}
</candidate_smt_snippet>


# === CHECKLIST ===
1. The SMT fragment faithfully encodes the natural‑language requirement.  
2. All new symbols follow the enforced naming conventions.  
3. No meaningful entity or qualifier is missing.  
4. The snippet introduces no symbol that duplicates one already present in the partial program.  

# === OUTPUT FORMAT ===
Reply only with a JSON object:
{{
    "faithful": true|false,
    "naming_ok": true|false,
    "entities_and_qualifiers_attended": true|false,
    "no_redeclare": true|false,
    "overall_ok": true|false,
    "explanations": {{
    "faithful": "...brief rationale...",
    "naming_ok": "...brief rationale...",
    "entities_and_qualifiers_attended": "...brief rationale...",
    "no_redeclare": "...brief rationale..."
    }}
}}